course: dictionary
lesson: 14996
title: Repulsive: very unpleasant
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Repulsive means very unpleasant, so much that it makes you feel sick or disgusted. «The smell from the rubbish bin was repulsive.» You would hold your nose and step back, and that tells you what the word means.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The slimy green soup was so repulsive that nobody would taste it.» Nobody wanting to taste it shows that people really hate it. Ask yourself what would fit in that place, then try a word like disgusting in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Be kind when you use this word. Repulsive is good for describing things like food, smells or slime, and monsters or behaviour in stories. Calling a person repulsive is hurtful, so do not say it about your classmates.
explain: In science, repulsive has a different meaning. Two magnets with like poles push each other apart, and this push is called repulsive force. In school this idea is often called repel, so check which subject you are reading.
fact: Repulsive means very unpleasant, making you feel sick or disgusted.
fact: «A repulsive smell» is a smell so bad that you want to move away from it.
fact: «Utterly repulsive» means completely disgusting, because utterly makes the word stronger.
fact: Repulsive is an adjective. Its forms are more repulsive and most repulsive.
fact: In science, repulsive describes a push between two like magnetic poles, which makes them move apart.
exercise: «The smell from the rubbish bin was repulsive.» What does repulsive mean here? | *Very unpleasant, making you feel sick | Very quiet | Bright and shiny | Sweet and lovely
exercise: «The monster had slime dripping from its teeth and was utterly repulsive.» Find and copy one word that tells you the monster was very unpleasant. | monster | *repulsive | story | teeth
exercise: Two like magnets push each other apart. What is this push called in science? | *Repulsive force | Sunshine | Gravity | Friction
test: «Mia said the soup looked repulsive.» What does repulsive mean? | Hot and steamy | Very tiny | *Disgusting | Lovely to look at
test: Which sentence about a friend is kind? | You smell repulsive today. | *Your painting is lovely. | You are repulsive.
exam: «The bin lorry left a repulsive smell on the street.» Which word is closest in meaning to repulsive? | Wet | Pleasant | Tiny | *Disgusting
